sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-054-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 388-393: Archaeopteryx -> Apatornis pelvis by equidistant coordinate-grid interpolation — MorphoEval overall 83.1/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 (v2), overall 83.1/100 (up from 68.8 in Pass 1). The five Fig. 393 silhouettes are segmented and landmarked from the SHA-256-pinned IA scan; GPA; Thompson's equidistant interpolation phi_t = (1-t) id + t phi (E2/E6) is run with phi as (i) a dense semilandmark TPS, (ii) a 9-anchor coarse TPS grid and (iii) an affine map (E5), and scored against Heilmann's drawn intermediates with the nearest-endpoint null. Heilmann's stages sit at t* = 0.263 / 0.529 / 0.824 (nominal 0.25 / 0.5 / 0.75; max residual 0.074; sweep SD <= 0.003 over 24 settings). Dense interpolation: Procrustes 0.134 / 0.121 / 0.093 vs endpoint 0.214 / 0.312 / 0.145 and affine 0.162 / 0.199 / 0.293; IoU 0.572 / 0.599 / 0.683 vs endpoint 0.538 / 0.436 / 0.629; r = 0.991-0.996; KS p <= 5.5e-6; correspondence-shift null exact p = 0.0104 (z = -4.4). The dense TPS folds as a grid (min det -10.4 inside the form) whereas the 9-anchor coarse grid is fold-free (min det 0.23) and beats the endpoint on stages 1-2 only. Part B (\"biologically real\") remains untestable; Dryad k1v34cf is a labelled variable mismatch. Verdict in result.json: mixed (A supported, approximately equidistant; B untestable). Overall 83.1/100 (faithfulness 82.3, reproducibility 85.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 7a7c0f5b6; environment: python 3.12, numpy 1.26.4, scipy 1.x (pip, requirements.txt lower bound >=1.7), scikit-image >=0.19, matplotlib >=3.3, Pillow >=8.0, lean 4.35.0 (elan stable). Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 82. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_054_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-054_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py at 7a7c0f5b6, image/png, 1061469 B, 2200×1350 px, artifact_sha256 a30bd5dd44fca70310c403159b0b7fe6a6aac573b8c9c82afc5364edd5894b2d (sha256 a30bd5dd44fca70310c403159b0b7fe6a6aac573b8c9c82afc5364edd5894b2d), spec_fingerprint 2777b4737ea8977ede0d810eac8e3fa1010e0a04c769590e31a7cb66eaa76bf4. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2777b4737ea8977ede0d810eac8e3fa1010e0a04c769590e31a7cb66eaa76bf4; artifact_sha256: a30bd5dd44fca70310c403159b0b7fe6a6aac573b8c9c82afc5364edd5894b2d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/apatornis_celer_holotype_synsacrum_marsh1880.jpg=28213a31e4c88718..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/archaeopteryx_lithographica_berlin_specimen_mfn.jpg=96341aed3d81b2b6..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/dryad_k1v34cf_deeming_mayr_2018_metadata.json=4f2b721ee3bec249..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/ongrowthform1917thom_p757_leaf0776_figs388-389.jpg=5214f00748cee71c..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/ongrowthform1917thom_p758_leaf0777_figs390-391.jpg=3b7d8054e6d7e995..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/ongrowthform1917thom_p759_leaf0778_fig392.jpg=17283e61fc562441..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/ongrowthform1917thom_p760_leaf0779_fig393.jpg=0e73dc9e37ed7e64..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/paper_citations.bib=6a29f62000543207..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/scout_manifest.json=6a8a3e51bdde2a4a..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-054/t1917_054_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_reference.json=92bc0f5512fe8f9d...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-054-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Fig. 388 Archaeopteryx pelvis in Cartesian coordinates; Fig. 389 Apatornis pelvis in a transformed grid (p. 757) | three intermediate and equidistant coordinate systems interpolated between them (p. 759, Fig. 390) | a pelvis outline inscribed in each interpolated system (Figs. 391-392) and the five-form series (Fig. 393) | the intermediates are 'hypothetical types' / 'transitional stages' (pp. 757, 759); reconstructed_in_script: the grid phi as a thin-plate spline on automatically detected landmarks + arc-length semilandmarks (dense) or on 9 anatomical anchors (coarse); Fig. 389's grid lines are not digitised | the stage parameter t and all statistics (t*, Procrustes, IoU, boundary RMSE, r, KS, permutation and correspondence nulls, Jacobian check) | segmentation of the wash drawings (Otsu, opening/closing) and the tip classification rule; transfer_boundary: the registered claim's 'biologically real intermediate forms' goes beyond Thompson's 'hypothetical types'; tested only against Heilmann's own drawn intermediates | the Berlin specimen bone/matrix segmentation is descriptive and enters no statistic of the verdict; does_not_claim: that the interpolated pelves match any real intermediate Mesozoic bird (part B untestable here) | any phylogenetic position for Apatornis beyond Clarke (2004) | that Heilmann's Fig. 393 series is drawn to one scale (centroid size is non-monotone) | that the dense semilandmark TPS is a valid coordinate grid (it folds; the coarse grid is)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=2.5]: Independent second assessor from a different provider",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.5]: Part B: 2-D pelvis landmarks of phylogenetically intermediate taxa (Jeholornis, Sapeornis, Confuciusornis, Enantiornithes, Hesperornis, Ichthyornis) to test whether the interpolated stages are biologically real",
            "remediation needed: R1 (open): independent second assessor from a different provider — this round is builder-scored",
            "remediation needed: R7: digitise the grid lines of Figs. 388-390 directly and compare Thompson's drawn intermediate grids with the fitted coarse TPS grid",
            "remediation needed: R8: part B — assemble 2-D pelvis landmarks of real intermediate Mesozoic birds from open literature plates (e.g. Marsh 1880 Ichthyornis/Hesperornis, PD) and test the interpolated stages against them",
            "remediation needed: R9: sweep the coarse-grid anchor count (5, 9, 13, 17) to locate where a fold-free grid starts to reproduce the drawn stages as well as the dense correspondence" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.831"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (builder-assessor, single-agent Pass 2; second assessor pending)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

